case-organizer (3.5) stable; urgency=medium

  * Added PDF Editing Tools hub with tool landing page + individual tool pages.
  * Merge PDF: allow adding PDFs across multiple file-picks/drag-drops, show a
    removable file list, and support drag/drop ordering using first-page
    thumbnails before merging.
  * Rearrange PDF Pages: A4 thumbnail tiles with drag/drop ordering and preview
    now updates to the reordered output PDF after applying changes.
  * Replaced Sign PDF with Flatten PDF (qpdf-based annotation flattening).
  * Added cancel workflow: Start button becomes Cancel once a job starts; Cancel
    clears the UI and marks the job canceled server-side.
  * Added ephemeral PDF job storage with auto-delete 5 minutes after completion
    (UI shows remaining time).
  * Rebuilt PDF compression with Rectal (lossless text-heavy) and Photon (lossy
    image-heavy) modes plus explicit size delta messaging.
  * Added Remove PDF Pages with range/odd/even/visual modes and post-apply
    preview of the cleaned PDF.
  * Added Page Numbers tool with range selection, position preview, and font
    controls for size, family, and color.
  * Added image-to-PDF conversion with thumbnail ordering and preview panel.
  * Added OCR PDF with Tesseract language picker, DPI control, and binarize
    option.
  * OCR: show full language names, provide DPI presets (192/288/384), and use
    adaptive binarization for cleaner scans; Debian dependencies updated for
    Tesseract/PDF rendering.
  * Fixed OCR language search filtering in the picker.
  * Added an extra half-inch top margin to invoice PDFs for letterhead space.

 -- Izumi <swarajswarupaggarwal@gmail.com>  Tue, 16 Dec 2025 03:35:00 +0530

case-organizer (3.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * Added a JSON "interpreter" view for Note.json, rendering structured case
    notes into a readable layout while preserving raw JSON editing when
    needed.
  * Introduced a unified Case Notes / Case Law Brief editor powered by the
    same interpreter, so both workflows share identical view/edit behaviour.
  * Added Case Law upload + search flows with per-case brief notes.
  * UI polish: Account dropdown menu now opens as a proper vertical list,
    right-aligned to the trigger, and correctly hides when collapsed.
  * Dev UX: Static CSS/JS links are cache-busted via mtime query params to
    ensure UI updates appear immediately even with long cache headers.

 -- Izumi <swarajswarupaggarwal@gmail.com>  Mon, 15 Dec 2025 19:45:00 +0530

